  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "0zksScWKfXIr7Ec+7by1RQO/qMg=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:33:11.923Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "STP house was added to the Flowable Partner Finder on 2026-08-14 and mined four days later, on 2026-08-18 \u2014 the newest entry in the sweep. Checking it produced a poor result: the site is inconsistent and the contact page 404s to a 2019 theme.\n\nDirectory freshness is not verification, and this row is the clearest demonstration of it. A partner card can be created the moment a commercial arrangement is signed, well before the firm has a maintained public presence to support it, and a contact page that fails while resolving to a six-year-old theme is evidence of a site nobody is tending. The listing therefore claims more currency than anything behind it.\n\nThat makes this the strongest argument in the sweep for treating the Partner Finder as a list of leads to verify rather than a qualified pipeline. The firm is excluded on geography in any case \u2014 it is based in Netanya, outside the EU scope \u2014 but the verification failure is the part that generalises to the other entries.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- STP house (IL Netanya) \u2014 stphouse.com\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Non-EU. Newest directory entry (added 2026-08-14); site inconsistent, /contact 404s to a 2019 theme \u00b7 SOURCE: Flowable Partner Finder (flowable.com/company/partners), mined 2026-08-18. NOT imprint-swept.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:33:11.923388Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:33:11.923394Z"
    }
  },
